  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington is firing on all cylinders. Yesterday's 17% revenue lift on 6 active groomers\u2014$538 per groomer, 8% above your 30-day baseline\u2014reflects both solid capacity utilization and disciplined upselling: add-on attachment jumped from 32% to 59%, and retail nearly doubled. Week-to-date is down 13%, but that's a calendar artifact; you had fewer appointments (47 vs 53) because Monday was lighter. Month-to-date sits at flat (+1%) against a DOW-adjusted expectation of -0.8%, meaning real performance is tracking slightly ahead. Year-to-date remains exceptional at +52% revenue and +53% appointments. Bather hours were zero yesterday\u2014a gap worth monitoring given trailing-30-day average of 4.9h/day\u2014but today's schedule recovers with 7 bather hours. Inventory is stable; top priority is X-Small Treat Table (zero stock, 30 monthly velocity) and Peanut Butter Cups (backlog of 15 units).\n\nHicksville is a smaller boat, but it's moving faster. Yesterday's 31% grooming revenue lift on just 2 active groomers ($450 per groomer, up 14% from baseline) is strong. Month-to-date sits at +8.4% against DOW-adjusted expectation, meaning real operational performance is outpacing calendar. However, retail dropped 27% despite higher transaction count, and add-on attach is anemic at 10%\u2014this is a front-of-house and upsell opportunity. The concerning signal: 12+ week visit gap is growing (8.4% to 10.2%), an early indicator of customer drift; combined with zero bather hours and a 1.9-groomer-day average, capacity constraints may be pushing customers toward longer intervals. The lapse pool of 58 customers ($40K annual value) is reactivation-ready.\n\nJuneteenth hits Friday; expect a 10% revenue dip. Port Washington has 6 groomers scheduled today and 5 tomorrow; Hicksville holds at 2 each day. Seven-day outlook: Port Washington 30 groomer-days, Hicksville 10 groomer-days\u2014Port Washington is carrying the load."
